"""StarlingX Provider Adapter — Phase 28E.

Minimal read-only StarlingX integration.

Architecture:

    StarlingX
        ↓
    StarlingXProviderAdapter (composes API + CLI collectors)
        ↓
    RawProviderSnapshot
        ↓
    [StarlingXProviderNormalizer → Canonical Domain Model]

Components:
    1. StarlingXAPICollector — 6 confirmed REST endpoints (GET-only, Keystone auth)
    2. StarlingXCLICollector — 3 confirmed CLI commands (allow-list, no arbitrary exec)
    3. StarlingXProviderAdapter — composes both, returns RawProviderSnapshot

Confirmed REST endpoints (Phase 28D live investigation):
    1. GET :18002/v1/alarms            (FM alarms — 9 fields per alarm)
    2. GET :18002/v1/event_log          (FM event log — singular, NOT /v1/events)
    3. GET :6385/v1/isystems            (sysinv system info)
    4. GET :6385/v1/ihosts              (sysinv hosts)
    5. GET :6385/v1/ihosts/{uuid}/imemorys  (sysinv memory, sub-resource)
    6. GET :7777/v1/nodes/              (smapi nodes)

Confirmed CLI commands (Phase 28D live investigation):
    1. fm alarm-show <uuid>  (7 CLI-only fields)
    2. system health-query    (platform health summary)
    3. software list           (USM release info)

Excluded (not confirmed or returns empty):
    - USM REST API (port 5492) — returns empty even with valid token
    - VIM REST API (port 4545) — deferred
    - Write operations (acknowledge, lock/unlock, etc.)

Safety:
    - GET-only REST; CLI allow-list; no tokens in logs/fixtures
    - Live validation NOT performed — fixture-based testing only
"""
